OpenOMF for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
===================================

Version @VERSION@.

OpenOMF, the open source engine for the 1994 fighting game One Must Fall
2097, built for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU. It draws the game's own
256-colour pictures straight onto an AGA screen through ACGame.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU.
- AGA, or an RTG board (SetEnv ACGame/Display RTG).
- One Must Fall 2097's data. It is freeware: the Installer downloads it
  from omf2097.com (needs C:Atlas and a network), or copies it from your
  own copy.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive anywhere (on AmiCradle: SYS:Utilities/OpenCompress x
openomf-...lha RAM:), then double-click Install-OpenOMF beside the
OpenOMF drawer. It asks where the game goes (Work:Games by default),
then fetches or copies the One Must Fall 2097 data into resources/.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the openomf icon. The keyboard plays both players; the
  game's own menus set the keys.

What this build leaves out
--------------------------

- Sound and music: this build has only OpenOMF's silent audio back end.
  An AHI back end is the next step.
- Network play.

This is a release candidate: it has been built, not yet played through
on a lab. Report problems at https://github.com/DalsinAI/amigaopenomf.

